// R2 skill-eval cases. One JSON object per line (blank lines and // comments skipped).
// lane=fast  -> exercised by the deterministic CI layer (TestOfflineSkillEval) AND the selection layer.
// lane=diagnosis|agent|boundary -> exercised by the opt-in real-model selection layer only (TestSelectionSkillEval, -model).
// boundary cases assert expected_intent + forbidden_skills so new skills cannot steal nearby how-to / FAQ questions.
// Questions mimic real CompShare user phrasing (colloquial, problem-driven, run-on) — calibrated against 聊天记录.md,
// NOT engineer-template "查询X / X怎么配置". They are paraphrases, never byte-equal to a skill's triggers, so the
// selection layer is non-tautological. The GPU model token (4090 / A100) is kept verbatim because the fast-tier
// pricing/specs handlers extract it from the raw question text.
